# promise: #807
# A click outside the ⌘T bar right after it opens closes it, as in Arc. Cra took the keys back from anything
# in the bar's first 0.6 s (meant for a page made behind it taking them), so a quick click was undone and the
# bar stayed open (GitHub #807, joodaloop, 0.1.56; likely also #722's one-off). The click here is real, through
# the window server, and the log says it came inside those 0.6 s.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
pace 0.05
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=quick-click
wait 2
cra://debug?mainFrame=100,100,1000,700
wait 1
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
click page-top
wait 1
cra://commandbar
click sidebar-empty
expect-log command bar lost the keys 0\.[0-5][0-9] s after opening to a click
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=after
expect-log Cra command bar rows after: open=0
